ancial literacy, health and wellbeing.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(PBS-HE, SBA-HE)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-CEL)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "This is a Learning Where You Live course.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": ["Students will be able to identify daily activity patterns and develop strategies for improving physical well-being; and identify sleep patterns and practice skills for improving sleep.", "Students will be able to identify healthy diets, poor eating patterns, and strategies for improving nutrient intake; and develop a plan for regular medical consultations and life-preserving tests/vaccines.", "Students will be able to develop a plan for personal budgeting, investing, and debt management.", "Students will be able to discuss and practice personal responsibility for health and sexual well-being, and identify techniques for stress reduction and maintenance of emotional well-being.", "Students will be able to implement skills for the maintenance of healthy interpersonal relationships."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "CU", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2811, "crseId": 372217, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "UNILWYL", "catalogNbr": "1416", "titleShort": "Socially Just Leadership Devel", "titleLong": "Socially Just Leadership Development", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 18201, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "07:30PM", "timeEnd": "08:45PM", "startDt": "01/24/2022", "endDt": "04/11/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "pd327", "firstName": "Perdita", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Das-Humphrey"}, {"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "ajh299", "firstName": "Andrew", "middleName": "J.", "lastName": "Hicks"}], "pattern": "M", "facilityDescr": "Hans Bethe House 240", "bldgDescr": "Hans Bethe House", "facilityDescrshort": "BET240", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Enrollment preference given to: residents of the West Campus House System. This is a Learning Where You Live course."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/24/2022", "endDt": "04/11/2022", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 1, "unitsMaximum": 1, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "SUS", "gradingBasisShort": "Sat/Unsat", "gradingBasisLong": "Satisfactory/Unsatisfactory", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/24/2022", "sessionEndDt": "05/21/2022", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "\"Socially Just Leadership Development\" will provide students an opportunity to use an enhanced social justice lens to nurture their leadership development and push past performative allyship. This interactive 12-week class will challenge students to reflect critically on their identities, learn the path from diversity to inclusion and justice, develop tangible skills and tools to interrupt injustice, and further their learning and understanding of social justice. Students will engage in small and large group discussions, guided activities, and will submit a reflection paper at the end of the semester to outline tangible action steps they can take in their time at Cornell and beyond.", "catalogBreadth": 